    {
      "id": "P2-001",
      "priority": "P2",
      "title": "The future blank form is content-constrained but not fully byte-deterministic from the sealed contract alone.",
      "evidence": [
        "The preregistration requires deterministic blanks and identifies fixed identities, constants, null execution-binding fields, key order, and one trailing newline.",
        "It does not fix the exact placeholder representation for every unfilled judgment field, such as omission versus null, or define a dedicated blank-conformance schema or validator.",
        "The later execution seal will still bind the actual blank raw bytes, and completed schema plus cross-file validation prevents silent identity substitution."
      ],
      "impact": "Two compliant custodians could produce byte-different neutral blanks, and neutrality is a required post-GO inspection rather than a fully mechanical construction proof. The actual-SHA execution seal contains the variance and therefore this does not reopen either P1 or block methodology GO.",
      "recommendedRemediation": [
        "Before distribution, use one exact blank template or a dedicated blank validator that fixes allowed keys, static consts, placeholder representation, forbidden content, key order, and trailing newline.",
        "Record the validator result together with the materialized blank hashes before creating the execution seal."
      ],
      "blocksGo": false
    }
